# ============================================================================
# CODEOWNERS — review routing (GOV-05, repository governance)
#
# Every pull request that touches the paths below automatically requests a
# review from the owning maintainer(s), so nothing lands in a lane nobody
# watches. This is the review half of the governance pair; the enforcement
# half is the `main-branch-protection` ruleset (GOV-01: PRs only, linear
# history, blocking CI gate).
#
# Why `require_code_owner_review` stays OFF in the ruleset: this is a
# single-maintainer repository — the PR author cannot approve their own PR,
# so a *required* code-owner review would deadlock every change until a
# second maintainer exists. CODEOWNERS still routes the review request;
# the merge gate stays the green CI gate (GOV-01).
#
# When additional maintainers join, split the global rule into per-lane
# owners (engine / app / infra) and flip `require_code_owner_review` on.
# ============================================================================

